# RGJ-RC1-011C — pinned RMS safe baseline
# Source pin: TASEmulators/freej2me-plus@13ec186903087156c145268f8706eecfaf9f1e50
#
# This contract SUPERSEDES the application of patches/0009-recordstore-rg35xx-storage-policy.patch
# for the RC1 pinned source. It does not delete 0009; historical Beta 5 intent remains recorded.
#
# Exact pinned RecordStore persistence model
# ------------------------------------------
# - <basename>.rms stores JSON metadata, IDs and tags.
# - <basename>.<recordId> stores each record payload separately.
# - saveRecordStore() rewrites metadata and all current record payload files.
# - addRecord/deleteRecord/setRecord currently call saveRecordStore() synchronously.
#
# RC1 decision
# ------------
# 1. KEEP the pinned upstream synchronous mutation->saveRecordStore() path for RC1.
# 2. DO NOT apply the Beta-5 single-target snapshot/atomic-replacement design to this
#    multi-file persistence format. A single-file temp/backup helper cannot make the
#    metadata + N payload files one atomic transaction.
# 3. KEEP RG35XXRmsCoordinator and RG35XXRmsAtomicFile source-controlled for rollback/
#    future work, but do not connect pinned RecordStore to markDirty()/flushRG35XX().
# 4. RG35XXRmsCoordinator.forceFlush() must remain a zero-cost/no-thread no-op when no
#    store has activated the coordinator. This lets lifecycle barriers remain harmless.
# 5. KEEP upstream RecordStore IDs, tags, versions, authentication, suite/vendor naming,
#    legacy migration and on-disk format unchanged.
# 6. Do not change the pinned RecordStore format merely to regain asynchronous writes.
# 7. Performance optimization of multi-file RMS is deferred until a generation/commit
#    protocol is explicitly designed, recovery-audited and device-tested.
#
# Why this is safer
# -----------------
# Applying the old single-file atomic helper to only <basename>.rms would allow metadata
# to commit independently of record payload files. Applying it separately to every file
# still would not create an all-or-nothing transaction across the set. Power loss or
# process termination between replacements could expose mixed generations.
#
# BUILD/DEVICE status
# -------------------
# STATIC-AUDIT-PASS is permitted for this policy once exact pinned call sites and helper
# behavior are audited. BUILD-PASS requires the consolidated pinned source to compile.
# DEVICE-TEST-PASS requires real RG35XX save/reopen/game-switch validation.
